Beryllium: rename the user-visible WebUI scheme helium:// to beryllium://

Purpose: Helium shows its WebUI pages under helium:// (helium://settings,
  helium://setup). Beryllium shows them under beryllium:// (owner decision
  Q11, 1 November 2026). Internally every page stays chrome://, exactly as
  in Helium: helium/core/override-chrome-protocol.patch maps the display
  scheme to chrome:// on navigation and chrome:// back to the display scheme
  in the omnibox, status bubble, hover card, copied URLs and tab search.
  This patch only changes the display scheme's value, so all of that
  machinery, and every security registration Helium gives the scheme
  (standard, secure, CORS, service worker, display-isolated, no javascript:
  URLs, WebUI), now applies to "beryllium" instead of "helium".
  helium:// is not kept as an alias: an alias would need a second set of
  scheme registrations, and Beryllium has no existing helium:// bookmarks.
  Typing helium:// behaves like any other unknown scheme.
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series), applied after helium/patches/series.
Depends on: helium/core/override-chrome-protocol.patch.
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca).
Not covered here: user-visible strings in .grd/.xtb files, which
  helium/utils/name_substitution.py rewrites from chrome:// to helium://.
  Beryllium's string substitution step must map helium:// to beryllium://
  after it runs.
Test: freebsd/tests/functional (planned): beryllium://settings and
  beryllium://setup load and the omnibox shows beryllium://; the address bar,
  copied URL, hover card and tab search show beryllium://, never helium://;
  typing chrome://settings still works and is displayed as beryllium://;
  a web page cannot navigate to or embed beryllium://settings (blocked like
  chrome://); helium://settings does not open a WebUI page.
security-review: required (changes the value of a registered WebUI scheme)

--- a/chrome/browser/resources/tab_search/tab_search_item.ts
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/tab_search/tab_search_item.ts
@@ -216,8 +216,8 @@
 
     // Show chrome:// if it's a chrome internal url
     const protocol = new URL(normalizeURL(data.tab.url)).protocol;
-    if (protocol === 'chrome:' || protocol === 'helium:') {
-      this.$.secondaryTextInner.prepend(document.createTextNode('helium://'));
+    if (protocol === 'chrome:' || protocol === 'beryllium:') {
+      this.$.secondaryTextInner.prepend(document.createTextNode('beryllium://'));
     }
   }
 
--- a/components/omnibox/browser/builtin_provider.cc
+++ b/components/omnibox/browser/builtin_provider.cc
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
     for (const std::u16string& url :
          client_->GetBuiltinsToProvideAsUserTypes()) {
       DCHECK(url.starts_with(u"chrome://"));
-      AddBuiltinMatch(std::u16string(url).replace(0, 6, u"helium"),
+      AddBuiltinMatch(std::u16string(url).replace(0, 6, u"beryllium"),
                       std::u16string(), styles);
     }
   } else {
